{
  "info": {
    "name": "Provisr API",
    "description": "Provisr orchestrator API — Week 1 endpoints.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this collection plus `provisr.env.json` (File → Import).\n2. Start the orchestrator: `task dev:orchestrator` (default http://localhost:4000).\n3. Pick an auth method:\n   - Real Clerk token: paste a session JWT into `bearerToken`.\n   - Dev bypass: set `AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=true`, `NODE_ENV=development`, `DEV_USER_ID=<id>` in `orchestrator/.env`, and set the same id in `devUserId`. The bypass is never honored in production.\n4. SSE routes cannot send headers from the browser's EventSource, so they read the token from the `?token=` query param (`sseToken`).\n\n## Notes\n- All IDs are UUIDs; the prefilled values in the environment are dummy UUIDs. Replace them with real IDs once the read/write endpoints return data.\n- Almost every protected endpoint currently answers `501 NOT_IMPLEMENTED` (OR-004/OR-005/OR-025 in progress). The test scripts encode that current behavior — flip them to success expectations as implementations land.\n- Error envelope: `{ error, message, status, code, request_id, details }`.\n- Mutations carry an `Idempotency-Key` header (AGENTS.md rule: every mutation needs an idempotency key).\n- CLI automation: `newman run Provisr_API.postman_collection.json -e provisr.env.json`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000" },
    { "key": "bearerToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "sseToken", "value": "" },
